Package: coreletd
Architecture: linux-any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends},
         adduser
Description: MeshCore daemon for the ClockworkPi uConsole with AIO v2
 coreletd drives the SX1262 LoRa transceiver on the HackerGadgets /
 OpenSourceSDRLab AIO v2 expansion board directly over spidev and libgpiod,
 speaks the MeshCore mesh protocol, and exposes the companion protocol over
 TCP so the MeshCore phone/web app, meshcore-cli and meshtui can connect --
 including from the uConsole itself over loopback.
 .
 It handles adverts and contacts, encrypted direct messages with acks,
 retries and path learning, and channel (group) messages. Repeater and room
 server roles are not implemented, and TCP is the only companion transport.
 .
 This is a clean-room C++20 implementation, not affiliated with MeshCore
 upstream. It needs a frequency configured for your region and an antenna
 fitted before it will transmit, so the service is not enabled on install.
